WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.435
-Welcome, everybody!
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.438
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.040
[ Applause ]

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.843
Well, guys, it is the last night
of Donald Trump's presidency.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:11.977
And...

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:15.248
[ Band plays,
cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.583
I don't know what
tomorrow's gonna feel like.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.118
Probably like that moment

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.387
when they pull the nasal swab
out of your nose.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.590
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.391
At least Trump
is leaving on top.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:28.227
I mean, Washington D.C. has
never looked more beautiful.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.930
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.665
Actually, that has nothing to do
with the riots.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.668
Those are just some of Melania's
old Christmas decorations.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.670
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.104
Yep, one more night.

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:41.574
For most Americans, it feels
like the night of Thanksgiving

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.410
when you're just staring at
your aunt and uncle thinking,

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.446
"Go home."

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:49.415
I think everyone is ready
for Trump to move on.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.417
This afternoon, even
the Lincoln Memorial stood up

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:52.418
and helped Trump pack.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.420
He's like, "I got it, I got it."

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.655
Some people are sad
to see Trump go.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:59.092
Earlier today, the movers
shook his hand and said,

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.161
"We've never moved so many
people out of their offices

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.261
in four years.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:03.496
You put our kids
through college.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.364
Thank you."

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.666
It was a touching scene
at the White House tonight,

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.469
especially when Trump's four
remaining staffers toasted him

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:12.438
by raising a glass of bleach.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.106
I thought that was sweet.

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:16.008
Today, all of
the White House staffers

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.376
are signing
each other's yearbooks

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:18.878
with things like,
"Keep in touch,"

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.347
"Friends for life," and,
"I won't testify against you

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.450
if you don't testify
against me."

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.652
Well, tomorrow morning,
Trump's holding a farewell event

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.187
at Joint Base Andrews.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.655
I heard that
everyone who's invited

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:32.424
has to be there by 7:15 a.m.,

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:35.761
and they can each bring along
five people.

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:38.264
You know they're having trouble
filling seats

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.600
when they offer everyone
a plus-five.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.203
Never heard of a plus-five.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:47.507
"You can come if you want.
You can you bring 30 people."

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.508
But it sounds like
a great party.

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:52.177
I mean, guests have to arrive
by 7:15 in the morning

00:01:52.177 --> 00:01:54.280
on a Wednesday
in the middle of January

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.148
during a pandemic.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.051
Even Craigslist actors
were like, "Pass."

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:00.753
And this is true.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.288
The guest list is so thin,

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.690
even Anthony Scaramucci
got an invite.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.425
You know your party
is struggling

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:10.029
when it's half family and half
staff you fired four years ago.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:13.499
But today, Trump released
a pre-recorded farewell address

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.102
from the White House, and
here are some of the highlights.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.437
-Now as I prepare
to hand power over

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.406
to a new administration

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.242
at noon on Wednesday,

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.344
I want you to know that
the movement we started

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.179
is only just beginning.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:30.583
We did what we came here to do

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.852
and so much more.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.388
The world respects us again.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:39.125
Please don't lose that respect.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.228
-Yeah.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.863
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.232
Trump said, "We did
what we came here to do."

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.200
It's true. I remember
his big campaign promise

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.003
was, "Build part of a wall
and pay for it ourselves."

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.938
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:56.275
Yep, Trump also said,
"The world respects us again."

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.177
When he heard that,
Vladimir Putin was like,

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.313
"Yes, yes, is always good
to end with joke."

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:03.148
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:04.617
[ Applause ]

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.252
"Classic, Buddy. [ Laughs ]"

00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:08.721
But today wasn't all bad.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.357
There was actually some nice
news for Trump. Listen to this.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.327
-President Trump's youngest
daughter has a big announcement.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.895
Tiffany Trump
is getting married.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.429
The 27-year-old
took to Instagram

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:18.965
to announce her happy news.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.700
-Trump was so sweet.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.136
He was like, "This week
isn't about you, Tiffany!"

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.305
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:27.874
Asked what
she's most excited for,

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.409
Tiffany was like,
"Changing last names."

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.678
Some entertainment news.

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:35.014
Last night was an all-new
episode of "The Bachelor,"

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.416
and Serena had a one-on-one date
with Matt.

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:38.885
And the date was going well

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.886
until an unexpected visitor
showed up.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:42.154
Watch this.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.757
-The feelings that
I'm already having for you,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.559
like, throughout this experience
is like,

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.194
they're real.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:54.767
♪♪

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.735
[ Donkey brays ]

00:03:56.735 --> 00:03:59.072
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:05.377
-All that was missing
was a graphic that said,

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:08.648
"Donkey, age 7,
social media influencer."

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:11.450
Yep, now along with herpes,

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.853
"The Bachelor" has to worry
about foot-and-mouth disease.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.921
Hey, check this out.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.424
I saw that Nissan has designed
a new concept van

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.294
intended to serve as a mobile
office for remote workers.

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.295
Take a look at this.

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:24.630
Yeah. And this is cool.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.331
It comes with a bumper sticker
that says,

00:04:26.331 --> 00:04:28.100
"I didn't get custody."

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.203
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.741
Yep, Nissan
will release the car

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.143
right after everyone
is vaccinated

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.044
and returns to the office.

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:40.079
We have a great show.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.114 align:start size:88% position:13%
give it up for The Roots 
everybody. 

